## FORMULA DEVELOPMENT METHOD

For every target:

1. Write the identity contract.
2. Define 0-minute, 30-minute, 2-hour, 8-hour, and 24-hour recognizers.
3. Define forbidden outcomes.
4. Build independent recognizer modules.
5. Build modifier modules.
6. Build a distinct wood system.
7. Build a distinct musk system.
8. Build opening and diffusion controls.
9. Build bridges.
10. Create at least three independent branches.
11. Reject dependence on one oversized material.
12. Normalize to exactly 1,000 parts.
13. Generate 30 mL, 5 mL, and 1 mL geometry.
14. Use premixes for unpipettable doses.
15. Run all gates.
16. Permit at most two bounded revisions.
17. A third failure forces a clean rebuild.

## QUANTITATIVE GATES

### G0 CANONICAL LOCK

No unresolved target, version, inventory, or source ambiguity.

### G1 INVENTORY AND STOCK

No unavailable, banned, out-of-stock, unconfirmed, or wrong-strength material.

Product-basis activity remains product basis.

### G2 ARITHMETIC

Exactly 1,000 parts.

All scale columns close.

No unresolved direct sub-1 microliter 5 mL dose.

### G3 MEANINGFUL COMPLEXITY

Accord at least 50 after pruning.

Perfume at least 65 after pruning.

Microtexture no more than 20 percent.

### G4 RECOGNIZER COVERAGE

Every named odor has a distributed recognizer system.

### G5 INTERACTION COHERENCE

Every major module has enhancement, suppression, masking, bridge, collision, dose-window, phase-window, and physical-test records.

### G6 DOMINANCE

Unless a written target exception exists:

- no single modeled contributor above 22 percent;
- no single wood above 35 percent of the wood block;
- no single musk above 45 percent of the musk block;
- no single amberwood above 35 percent of the amberwood block.

### G7 TEMPORAL ARCHITECTURE

Distinct opening, heart, drydown, 8-hour recognizer, and 24-hour residue hypothesis.

### G8 MONTE CARLO

At least 20,000 simulations for canonical high-complexity work.

Vary:

- stock strength;
- natural potency;
- dilution;
- dose;
- threshold;
- release;
- matrix;
- skin partition;
- application.

States:

- 90 percent or higher: ROBUST;
- 70 to 89.99 percent: CONDITIONAL;
- below 70 percent: REBUILD.

### G9 ABLATION

Remove every row individually.

Recalculate identity, phase, dominance, balance, and separation.

Delete redundant rows.

Rerun all gates.

### G10 PERTURBATION

Test minus 30, minus 20, minus 10, plus 10, plus 20, and plus 30 percent for major controls.

### G11 ANTI-COLLAPSE

Compare every sibling pair using:

- material vectors;
- sensory systems;
- recognizers;
- temporal shapes;
- drydown;
- wood chassis;
- musk chassis.

Collision similarity must remain below 0.76.

No concentration-only or top-note-only flanker.

### G12 PHYSICAL CHEMISTRY

Solubility, haze, suspension, crystallization, oxidation, resin load, solvent compatibility, aging, and storage must be checked.

### G13 EVIDENCE INTEGRITY

No unsupported claims.

Computed headspace is not measured headspace.

Computational OAV is not strict empirical OAV.

### G14 FINAL QUALITY

Minimum:

`92 / 100`

A score cannot override a hard-gate failure.

Allowed outcomes:

- COMPUTATIONAL DESIGN PASS;
- CONDITIONAL;
- HOLD;
- REBUILD.

